# Copy to .env.local. `npx convex dev` writes the first two for you the first
# time it runs, so you rarely need to fill those in by hand.
#
# Everything in this file is Next-side: it is read at build time or in the
# browser. The Convex deployment has its own, separate environment — see the
# block at the bottom.

# Which Convex deployment the CLI talks to, e.g. `dev:limber-panda-123`.
CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT=

# The deployment's client origin, e.g. `https://limber-panda-123.convex.cloud`.
# Read by the browser client and by `middleware.ts`.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL=

# Vercel Production only (do not copy into `.env.local`). The value must be a
# Convex production deployment key. While authenticated to Convex, create one
# with `npx convex deployment token create vercel-production --deployment prod`,
# then save its output directly as the Vercel secret without committing it:
#
#   CONVEX_DEPLOY_KEY   secret consumed by `npx convex deploy`
#
# On Vercel Production, the source-controlled build command deploys Convex
# first, then injects that deployment's URL into the nested Next.js build as
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL. Preview and other non-production builds run only
# `npm run build`; they deliberately never deploy or mutate Convex.
#
# Keep NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL configured in Vercel's Production environment as
# well, set to that same production deployment URL: the build command only
# injects it into the nested build, and the middleware and the `/api/auth`
# proxy it serves still read it from the environment at runtime.

# --- Which sign-in options the UI offers -----------------------------------
#
# The browser cannot read Convex deployment environment variables, so these
# two flags mirror what is configured over there. They only draw buttons; the
# providers themselves are switched on by the Convex-side keys below, and a
# flag set without its key gets you a control that fails.
#
# Set both sides, or neither. With neither, Margin is exactly the email +
# password sign-in and the 8-character invite codes it has always been.

# `1` shows "Continue with Google" on /signin. Needs AUTH_GOOGLE_ID/_SECRET.
NEXT_PUBLIC_AUTH_GOOGLE=

# `1` shows "Email me a sign-in link" on /signin and the invite-by-email form
# on the lab page. Needs RESEND_API_KEY.
NEXT_PUBLIC_AUTH_EMAIL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Set on the Convex DEPLOYMENT, not here.
#
# Inspect or change them with `npx convex env list` / `npx convex env set`.
#
# Convex Auth signs its own JWTs, so the deployment needs a key pair and the
# app's public origin. `npx @convex-dev/auth` generates and sets all three:
#
#   JWT_PRIVATE_KEY   PKCS#8 RS256 private key
#   JWKS              matching public JWK set
#   SITE_URL          http://localhost:3000 in dev
#
# SITE_URL is also where every sign-in link and every emailed invitation
# points, so a deployment sending mail must have it set to the real origin.
#
# Google sign-in. Both must be set or the provider is not registered at all.
# Create an OAuth 2.0 Web application client in the Google Cloud console and
# add `https://<your-deployment>.convex.site/api/auth/callback/google` as an
# authorized redirect URI — the callback lands on Convex, not on Next:
#
#   AUTH_GOOGLE_ID       OAuth client id
#   AUTH_GOOGLE_SECRET   OAuth client secret
#
# Sign-in links and emailed invitations, sent through the Resend HTTP API:
#
#   RESEND_API_KEY    required for both; without it neither is registered
#   AUTH_EMAIL_FROM   optional sender, e.g. `Margin <hello@yourdomain.edu>`.
#                     Defaults to Resend's `onboarding@resend.dev` sandbox
#                     sender, which only delivers to the Resend account owner
#                     — fine for development, wrong for anyone else.
#
# Post-session synthesis calls the OpenAI Responses API from a Convex action:
#
#   OPENAI_API_KEY      required for synthesis; without it the action fails
#                       with a clear error and everything else still works
#   SYNTHESIS_MODEL     optional model override (defaults in convex/synthesis.ts)
#   SCOUT_MODEL         optional model override for the scout's corpus runs
#                       (defaults in convex/delegations.ts). The scout uses the
#                       same OPENAI_API_KEY; without it a run fails with a
#                       reader-facing sentence and the brief is unaffected.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
